      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A fintech dashboard, you say? A great place for some cleverly designed interactive elements, but also a potential minefield for accessibility pitfalls. I'm glad you're thinking ahead, though - a well-designed dashboard can be a real game-changer for users. \n\nNow, let's get down to business. Here's a technical checklist to help you ensure your color contrast requirements are met and your interactive components are accessible to screen reader users:\n\n**Color Contrast Requirements:**\n\n1. **WCAG 2.1 Contrast Ratio:** Ensure that the contrast ratio between the background and foreground colors of all interactive elements (buttons, dropdowns, etc.) is at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 7:1 for larger text (18pt or 14pt bold).\n2. **Color Palette:** Choose a color palette that adheres to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 color contrast guidelines. You can use online tools like the WebAIM Color Contrast Checker or the WCAG Color Contrast Checker to test your color combinations.\n3. **Background and Text Colors:** Ensure that the background and text colors are not too similar in hue, saturation, or lightness. A good rule of thumb is to",
      "source": "target",
